<div class="guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Provider comparison">
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th scope="col">Provider</th>
<th scope="col">Compose with the shell</th>
<th scope="col">What differs from a host tool</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-gh">gh</a>
</th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Read PR metadata → filter with <code>jq</code> → comment with a separate grant.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">GitHub-shaped commands, not the GitHub CLI; no arbitrary API passthrough.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-ripgrep">ripgrep</a> / <a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-python">python</a>
</th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Search piped text or transform structured data in RustPython.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">Neither opens host files. Python exposes selected modules, not pip.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-curl">curl</a>
</th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Fetch an allowed HTTPS URL into a byte-stream pipeline.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">GET only; destination and byte limits still apply to model-chosen URLs.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-turso-sql">turso</a>
</th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Store and query records with the Rust Turso SQL engine.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">Broker-owned durable files; exceeding write budgets can leave a database unreadable.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-gpt-image">gpt-image</a>
</th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Generate or edit PNGs using a ChatGPT subscription.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">Separate broker-held subscription credentials; this provider does not use an OpenRouter key.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<th scope="row"><a href="https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon-provider-vm">vm / ssh</a></th>
<td data-label="Compose with the shell">Run browser or Python tools through a separately operated Linux/KVM vm-runner.</td>
<td data-label="What differs from a host tool">The command word is not SSH. The runner has its own VM boundary; it is not part of the native Mac installation.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
