<div class="workbench-example">
<div>
<h3>Read a PR, keep two fields</h3>
<p>Illustrative script for Dekopon’s <code>bash</code> tool, not your terminal. Replace the repository and PR number; install a compatible <code>gh</code> component and grant <code>gh.pull-request.read</code> first.</p>
</div>
<pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Illustrative read-only GitHub workflow"><code>set -e
set -o pipefail
gh pr view 7 -R owner/repo --json title,state | jq '{title, state}'</code>
</pre>
</div>
<p>The result is an object with <code>title</code> and <code>state</code>, not a file checkout. A missing session grant exits 127; a broker denial exits 126.</p>
<p>These providers ship separately. Install components compatible with the current <code>provider@0.4.0</code> contract and their required host interfaces; the core image does not bundle them. <a href="/providers/">Build and test a provider</a> · <a href="{{ site.repository }}/blob/main/docs/authorization.md">Configure access</a>
</p>
<h3>Jobs and reusable skills</h3>
<p>Routes can opt into bounded background jobs. Installed providers can run child scripts under the caller's existing limits, and agents with a storage grant can save learned skills. <a href="{{ release.sourceUrl }}/crates/dekopon-shell/README.md">See the runtime controls</a>.</p>
<p>Set per-agent token budgets in the gateway and inspect broker-granted commands through the optional <a href="{{ release.sourceUrl }}/crates/dekopon-console/README.md">packaged console ↗</a>. <a href="{{ site.repository }}/blob/main/docs/design.md#token-budgets">Token budgets ↗</a>.</p>
</div>
